OneTimeUseIdPolicy::checkAction
├── given the configId was never initialized
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the pinned id is unburned
│   ├── when the session's own burn led the batch in this transaction
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── when no burn was validated before this execution
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   ├── when only another session's burn was validated
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   ├── when the burn was validated under another multiplexer
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── when the burn was a consumeFor
│       ├── it should refuse a plain execution behind it
│       ├── it should approve a zero-value approve of PERMIT2 behind it
│       ├── it should refuse an approve of any other spender
│       ├── it should refuse an approve of PERMIT2 that carries value
│       ├── it should refuse an approve of PERMIT2 with bytes appended
│       ├── it should approve deposit() on the pinned wrapped native, with value
│       ├── it should refuse deposit() when no wrapped native was pinned
│       ├── it should refuse deposit() on any other target
│       ├── it should refuse any other selector on the pinned wrapped native
│       ├── it should refuse deposit() with bytes appended
│       ├── it should keep refusing plain executions when a wrapped native is pinned
│       └── it should keep refusing after a later consume in the same transaction
├── given the pinned id has been burned
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the burn happened in an earlier transaction
│   └── it should still return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the pinned id is shared with another action slot
│   └── when that id is burned
│       └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED from every slot pinned to it
├── given a batch of many executions in one settlement
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS for every one the burn led while unburned
├── it should never itself burn the id (it writes only the transient burn-approved flag)
├── given the call targets this policy with calldata shorter than a selector
│   └── it should fail closed and return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the call targets this policy and the selector is consume
│   ├── when the id argument is this session's OWN id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── when the id argument names ANOTHER session's id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── when the calldata is malformed (shorter than an id argument)
│       └── it should fail closed and return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the call targets this policy and the selector is consumeFor
│   ├── when the id argument is this session's OWN id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── when the id argument names ANOTHER session's id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── when the calldata is truncated (no witness word)
│       └── it should fail closed and return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the call is unrelated to this policy
│   └── when the session's burn led the batch
│       └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
└── given a deadline is pinned
    ├── when the deadline is in the future
    │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
    ├── when the current timestamp equals the deadline
    │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS (inclusive)
    ├── when the deadline has passed
    │   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
    │   ├── it should refuse the session's own consume op
    │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED even while the id is unburned
    └── when the deadline is zero
        └── it should never expire
